# <type>(<scope>): <what changed, imperative, ~72 chars>
#
# WHY the previous state was wrong — not a restatement of the diff. Git history is
# the record of change (AGENTS.md §4); a pull-request description does not replace
# this paragraph.
#
# Cover, when they apply:
#   * the argument — what was wrong, and why this is the right shape of fix
#   * alternatives rejected, and what ruled them out
#   * what you VERIFIED, with the numbers (suite counts, measurements, re-derived
#     figures) — never "tests pass"
#   * ⚠ traps and residuals a future reader needs, marked so they are skimmable
#
# `git commit -m "one line"` is insufficient by policy for anything non-trivial.
#
# ⚠ THE TRAILER BELOW IS A SECOND COPY OF THE FORMAT IN `PERSONA.md`, and a template
# cannot read a file — so a format change has to touch both. PERSONA.md is the source;
# if the two disagree, it wins and this line is the stale one. Fill in your registered
# name (mixed-case name, lowercase email) before you commit; the literal placeholder
# is not a valid trailer. `tests/test_commit_hygiene.py` checks both this template and
# the commit.
#
# ⚠ This template is INERT unless `commit.template` is set, and it is not set today
# (measured 2026-09-16).

Co-Authored-By: <Name> <<name-lowercase>@artificialhumanity.io>
